WEBVTT

1
00:00:30.198 --> 00:00:32.732
Previously on
Star Trek: Strange New Worlds...

2
00:00:32.866 --> 00:00:35.369
I'm in a relationship.
My life is complicated.

3
00:00:35.503 --> 00:00:36.704
Because Carol is pregnant.

4
00:00:36.837 --> 00:00:39.207
Maybe I could be someone

5
00:00:39.307 --> 00:00:40.808
who takes chances more often.

6
00:00:40.908 --> 00:00:42.643
Spock and I made it very clear
with each other.

7
00:00:42.710 --> 00:00:43.977
No complicated expectations.

8
00:00:44.044 --> 00:00:45.213
Just fun times.

9
00:00:48.382 --> 00:00:49.717
You punched a dinosaur?

10
00:00:49.850 --> 00:00:51.552
I broke my hand
and I don't feel any pain.

11
00:00:51.652 --> 00:00:53.421
My whole body
feels more attuned.

12
00:00:53.554 --> 00:00:55.589
- And your mind?
- Confused.

13
00:00:55.689 --> 00:00:57.057
Being Vulcan
affected you differently.

14
00:00:57.191 --> 00:00:58.692
You are aggressive.

15
00:00:58.792 --> 00:01:00.728
Are you going to try
and take over the galaxy now?

16
00:01:00.828 --> 00:01:02.496
I don't know.

17
00:01:23.584 --> 00:01:27.087
Personal log. Stardate 2903.9.

18
00:01:27.188 --> 00:01:28.989
The Future
Federation Leaders retreat

19
00:01:29.089 --> 00:01:31.024
was an overwhelming success.

20
00:01:31.091 --> 00:01:32.593
But my plan to hitch a ride home

21
00:01:32.726 --> 00:01:36.029
with fellow attendees
La'An and Spock has hit a snag.

22
00:01:36.130 --> 00:01:40.100
We detected a mysterious signal
in an uncharted region of space.

23
00:01:40.201 --> 00:01:43.103
It's the kind of thing
I joined Starfleet for.

24
00:01:43.204 --> 00:01:45.606
and yet for the first time.

25
00:01:45.739 --> 00:01:49.877
I can't shake the feeling
I'm in the wrong place.

26
00:01:51.212 --> 00:01:52.280
Curious.

27
00:01:52.380 --> 00:01:53.646
The signal is being broadcast

28
00:01:53.747 --> 00:01:55.348
over an old
Federation frequency.

29
00:01:55.449 --> 00:01:57.985
Spock. no one likes
a back seat sensor reader.

30
00:01:58.085 --> 00:01:59.720
Apologies.

31
00:02:02.290 --> 00:02:04.057
Is everything all right?

32
00:02:04.158 --> 00:02:07.295
At the retreat.
you seemed distracted.

33
00:02:07.395 --> 00:02:08.662
I'm fine.

34
00:02:11.665 --> 00:02:13.334
Now that we're closer.
can you pinpoint a signal?

35
00:02:13.434 --> 00:02:14.735
Sending coordinates.

36
00:02:14.802 --> 00:02:17.305
It's just behind
that larger asteroid there.

37
00:02:27.948 --> 00:02:29.417
My God. Is that...

38
00:02:29.517 --> 00:02:31.118
The Griffin.

39
00:02:32.520 --> 00:02:34.954
After all these years.

40
00:02:35.823 --> 00:02:37.525
Please tell me that there's...

41
00:02:38.459 --> 00:02:41.895
Sensors show
no life signs aboard.

42
00:02:44.465 --> 00:02:45.866
300 souls on board

43
00:02:45.999 --> 00:02:47.835
when she went missing
nine years ago.

44
00:02:47.935 --> 00:02:49.737
Last known location
light-years from here.

45
00:02:49.837 --> 00:02:52.840
Captain Taggert sent a report
to Starbase 1. and then...

46
00:02:52.940 --> 00:02:54.575
And then. the Griffin vanished.

47
00:02:54.675 --> 00:02:56.109
The most obvious explanation
was the Griffin

48
00:02:56.210 --> 00:02:57.545
was in the wrong place
at the wrong time.

49
00:02:57.645 --> 00:02:58.846
stumbled on a Klingon
Bird-of-Prey.

50
00:02:58.946 --> 00:03:00.448
its destruction covered up.

51
00:03:00.514 --> 00:03:02.350
A logical theory based
on its last known position

52
00:03:02.450 --> 00:03:03.884
is that a stellar flare
hit the Griffin

53
00:03:04.017 --> 00:03:05.219
while it entered warp.

54
00:03:05.319 --> 00:03:06.720
scattering it
over many light-years.

55
00:03:06.854 --> 00:03:08.456
That and every other theory
that Starfleet had

56
00:03:08.522 --> 00:03:10.724
doesn't explain
what we're looking at here.

57
00:03:12.360 --> 00:03:14.094
So. what the hell
really happened?

58
00:03:15.796 --> 00:03:17.731
Only one way to find out.

59
00:03:18.932 --> 00:03:20.301
Two flashlights. Really?

60
00:03:20.368 --> 00:03:22.002
You know. as soon as I'm back
on Enterprise.

61
00:03:22.069 --> 00:03:24.037
I'm gonna make sure
to reprimand whoever conducted

62
00:03:24.137 --> 00:03:25.806
the last inspection.

63
00:03:25.873 --> 00:03:27.541
Starting to see
why you and Spock are perfect

64
00:03:27.641 --> 00:03:28.909
for one another.

65
00:03:30.411 --> 00:03:31.545
Not to worry.

66
00:03:31.679 --> 00:03:35.048
I was a Boy Scout
before I was Starfleet.

67
00:03:38.786 --> 00:03:40.421
Be prepared. right?

68
00:03:43.557 --> 00:03:45.626
Stowaway?

69
00:03:47.328 --> 00:03:49.563
Gift. For my son.

70
00:03:49.663 --> 00:03:51.832
I was supposed to visit
this weekend. but then I got

71
00:03:51.899 --> 00:03:53.567
the call for the retreat
and I. uh...

72
00:03:53.667 --> 00:03:55.403
Couldn't pass up a chance to
meet Admiral Smillie in person.

73
00:03:55.503 --> 00:03:58.506
I've been studying his maneuvers
my whole career.

74
00:03:59.273 --> 00:04:01.742
Well. I am sure
David will understand

75
00:04:01.842 --> 00:04:04.845
as soon as he meets
his new little friend.

76
00:04:08.949 --> 00:04:10.784
Our discovery and coordinates
have been sent to Enterprise

77
00:04:10.918 --> 00:04:12.720
via long-range
transmission package.

78
00:04:12.786 --> 00:04:14.955
All right. then.

79
00:04:19.226 --> 00:04:21.261
Let's boldly go.

80
00:04:32.840 --> 00:04:34.942
Why aren't we floating?

81
00:04:36.610 --> 00:04:39.613
There is no scientific
reason this ship should have gravity.

82
00:04:41.349 --> 00:04:42.783
And yet...

83
00:04:42.916 --> 00:04:44.117
Well.

84
00:04:44.251 --> 00:04:47.355
that's unnerving
with a side of unsettling.

85
00:04:48.288 --> 00:04:49.757
I don't understand.

86
00:04:49.823 --> 00:04:52.058
It's like everyone
took a coffee break.

87
00:04:52.125 --> 00:04:54.061
And never returned.

88
00:05:00.233 --> 00:05:01.335
Do you hear that?

89
00:05:01.469 --> 00:05:03.604
I don't hear anything.

90
00:05:03.704 --> 00:05:05.506
No hum of a warp core.

91
00:05:05.639 --> 00:05:07.240
no buzzing from life support.
nothing.

92
00:05:07.307 --> 00:05:08.909
Readings
show no signs of radiation.

93
00:05:09.009 --> 00:05:12.646
virus. parasite or unusual
anomalies of any kind.

94
00:05:13.447 --> 00:05:15.349
For all intents and purposes.

95
00:05:15.449 --> 00:05:17.451
this ship is perfectly safe.

96
00:05:19.286 --> 00:05:20.654
Right.

97
00:05:20.788 --> 00:05:24.625
Show of hands for anyone
who feels safe on the Griffin?

98
00:05:27.160 --> 00:05:30.764
This appears to be the source
of the signal we detected.

99
00:05:32.299 --> 00:05:34.334
What's powering it?

100
00:05:36.203 --> 00:05:38.038
That is unclear.

101
00:05:41.975 --> 00:05:43.677
What did you do?

102
00:05:43.777 --> 00:05:45.579
I did nothing.

103
00:05:50.718 --> 00:05:53.120
This computer's last system
check indicates that all

104
00:05:53.220 --> 00:05:55.389
of the ship's power
should have expired years ago.

105
00:05:55.489 --> 00:05:57.957
So. it was asleep
and now it's awake?

106
00:05:59.026 --> 00:06:00.794
In a manner of speaking.

107
00:06:00.861 --> 00:06:02.496
Life support is now on line.

108
00:06:02.596 --> 00:06:04.565
But we have only one hour
before remaining power

109
00:06:04.665 --> 00:06:05.866
is drained for good.

110
00:06:05.966 --> 00:06:08.469
60 minutes to figure out
what happened here.

111
00:06:08.569 --> 00:06:10.237
Oxygen level is stable.

112
00:06:10.370 --> 00:06:12.372
We can remove our masks.

113
00:06:30.323 --> 00:06:32.392
No shuttlecraft.

114
00:06:32.526 --> 00:06:33.894
No escape pods.

115
00:06:33.994 --> 00:06:35.563
Is that how the crew evacuated?

116
00:06:35.696 --> 00:06:37.531
Possible.

117
00:06:37.598 --> 00:06:41.669
but there's no shuttle log
or reports of pods jettisoning.

118
00:06:41.735 --> 00:06:43.737
And there are no records
of unusual discoveries

119
00:06:43.837 --> 00:06:45.573
or experiments.

120
00:06:47.074 --> 00:06:48.876
There appears to be...

121
00:06:48.942 --> 00:06:51.411
No sign of anything wrong.

122
00:06:51.512 --> 00:06:52.780
So...

123
00:06:53.547 --> 00:06:55.082
where did everyone go?

124
00:06:57.317 --> 00:07:00.954
Perhaps answers can
only be uncovered by Division 12.

125
00:07:01.088 --> 00:07:02.355
Division 12?

126
00:07:02.422 --> 00:07:03.957
Starfleet analysts
that run around

127
00:07:04.057 --> 00:07:05.793
investigating
unexplained phenomena

128
00:07:05.893 --> 00:07:07.761
can have their turn
when we're done.

129
00:07:09.029 --> 00:07:10.664
We still have time to...

130
00:07:15.135 --> 00:07:16.504
Hello?

131
00:07:17.370 --> 00:07:18.639
Hello?

132
00:07:18.739 --> 00:07:21.041
We're here to help.

133
00:07:26.614 --> 00:07:28.849
I've been waiting for you.

134
00:07:30.117 --> 00:07:32.052
Wait.

135
00:07:54.041 --> 00:07:55.808
Space.

136
00:07:57.144 --> 00:07:59.179
The final frontier.

137
00:08:00.814 --> 00:08:04.585
These are the voyages
of the starship Enterprise.

138
00:08:06.720 --> 00:08:08.522
Its five-year mission:

139
00:08:08.622 --> 00:08:11.725
to explore strange new worlds...

140
00:08:13.861 --> 00:08:16.263
to seek out new life

141
00:08:16.363 --> 00:08:18.866
and new civilizations...

142
00:08:19.867 --> 00:08:24.004
to boldly go
where no one has gone before.

143
00:09:49.690 --> 00:09:52.559
There are no life signs present.

144
00:09:52.626 --> 00:09:54.695
It is as if the survivor
not only vanished.

145
00:09:54.762 --> 00:09:56.697
but was never here at all.

146
00:09:56.797 --> 00:10:00.000
Not enough power for her
to have transported out of here.

147
00:10:00.100 --> 00:10:02.636
Maybe she transported
before power was lost.

148
00:10:02.770 --> 00:10:04.738
I saw something like that
on the MLK.

149
00:10:04.805 --> 00:10:06.640
A landing party got caught
in the buffer.

150
00:10:06.774 --> 00:10:08.208
Engineering never got them out.

151
00:10:08.275 --> 00:10:09.810
An excellent theory.

152
00:10:09.910 --> 00:10:12.079
But readings show no signs
of any transmitted material.

153
00:10:12.179 --> 00:10:16.950
However. there are faint traces
of negatively charged ions.

154
00:10:17.050 --> 00:10:18.151
You mean a ghost?

155
00:10:18.285 --> 00:10:20.153
I mean negatively charged ions.

156
00:10:20.253 --> 00:10:22.422
The survivor we encountered
shed ions directly

157
00:10:22.522 --> 00:10:24.257
into this dead end.

158
00:10:24.324 --> 00:10:26.393
And then what?

159
00:10:26.459 --> 00:10:27.828
Drifted into space?

160
00:10:27.928 --> 00:10:29.830
This is where her trail ends.

161
00:10:29.930 --> 00:10:31.699
Let's find out where it began.

162
00:10:43.010 --> 00:10:44.678
What could cause someone

163
00:10:44.778 --> 00:10:47.815
to emit negatively charged ions?

164
00:10:47.915 --> 00:10:50.517
This ship presents
many scientific contradictions.

165
00:10:50.650 --> 00:10:54.221
I would need more evidence
before positing a cogent theory.

166
00:10:55.288 --> 00:10:57.758
Evidence like that?

167
00:11:05.733 --> 00:11:08.869
The survivor's trail began on
the other side of these doors.

168
00:11:10.337 --> 00:11:12.706
Those markings...
they're from phasers.

169
00:11:12.806 --> 00:11:15.108
These are Starfleet.

170
00:11:16.009 --> 00:11:18.511
And those are Klingon.

171
00:11:18.611 --> 00:11:20.748
And these Vulcan.

172
00:11:23.817 --> 00:11:26.019
I am beginning to suspect
we are not the first party

173
00:11:26.119 --> 00:11:28.055
to board the Griffin.

174
00:11:28.188 --> 00:11:30.390
One party tried
to seal someone in.

175
00:11:30.523 --> 00:11:32.259
another tried to blast them out.

176
00:11:32.359 --> 00:11:34.494
So what's behind those doors?

177
00:11:34.561 --> 00:11:36.063
Watch our six.

178
00:11:36.196 --> 00:11:38.265
Spock. help me with the door.

179
00:12:17.771 --> 00:12:19.406
James?

180
00:12:19.506 --> 00:12:21.274
You all right?

181
00:12:22.876 --> 00:12:25.378
Sorry.
Thought I heard something.

182
00:12:25.478 --> 00:12:27.380
but it was nothing.

183
00:12:29.016 --> 00:12:32.085
Right. Well.
we've loosened the barricades.

184
00:13:01.581 --> 00:13:04.717
Empty body bags.
Where did the bodies go?

185
00:13:04.784 --> 00:13:06.453
The medical transporter
is offline.

186
00:13:06.553 --> 00:13:08.055
I can reroute power
and check the records.

187
00:13:08.155 --> 00:13:09.489
but it will take time.

188
00:13:09.589 --> 00:13:11.624
Which we're running out of.
Let's split up.

189
00:13:11.758 --> 00:13:13.226
Spock. get those records.

190
00:13:13.326 --> 00:13:14.727
We'll head to the bridge
to see what we can find out

191
00:13:14.794 --> 00:13:16.229
about the survivor
and where she might be.

192
00:13:16.296 --> 00:13:18.298
Meet back here in 20 minutes.

193
00:13:23.603 --> 00:13:25.973
- Stay safe. okay?
- Likewise.

194
00:13:57.270 --> 00:13:59.706
You don't really believe
in ghosts. do you?

195
00:13:59.806 --> 00:14:03.410
No. but I'd love to give closure

196
00:14:03.510 --> 00:14:05.712
to the families
of the Griffin's crew.

197
00:14:05.845 --> 00:14:07.847
You're thinking
of Carol and David?

198
00:14:07.948 --> 00:14:10.217
What's David like?

199
00:14:10.350 --> 00:14:11.518
Hilarious.

200
00:14:11.651 --> 00:14:13.253
- Yeah?
- Beautiful. Happy.

201
00:14:13.353 --> 00:14:15.488
Takes after his mother
on all three.

202
00:14:15.588 --> 00:14:18.525
- And how is Carol?
- Oh. Carol's great.

203
00:14:18.625 --> 00:14:21.694
Incredible mom. Just got
approved for a dream project.

204
00:14:21.794 --> 00:14:24.631
Carol and I?

205
00:14:24.697 --> 00:14:26.433
Well...

206
00:14:28.501 --> 00:14:29.769
It's my fault really.

207
00:14:29.869 --> 00:14:32.239
She was never a fan
of Starfleet.

208
00:14:32.372 --> 00:14:36.309
Always worried I would die alone
somewhere in unknown space.

209
00:14:37.277 --> 00:14:40.680
No idea what would give her
that impression.

210
00:14:41.748 --> 00:14:43.150
Ah.

211
00:14:43.216 --> 00:14:47.020
I don't know how Sam balances
Starfleet and family.

212
00:14:47.087 --> 00:14:50.057
Well. I don't really
have that problem.

213
00:14:50.190 --> 00:14:52.692
Starfleet is my family.

214
00:14:56.563 --> 00:14:59.232
La'An. can I ask you something?

215
00:14:59.366 --> 00:15:01.268
Mm-hmm.

216
00:15:06.406 --> 00:15:08.341
No negatively charged ions.

217
00:15:09.409 --> 00:15:13.913
There's nothing
in this corridor but us.

218
00:15:14.714 --> 00:15:16.483
What were you going to ask me?

219
00:15:19.419 --> 00:15:21.354
Do you believe in ghosts?

220
00:15:22.755 --> 00:15:25.558
Not funny.

221
00:15:33.333 --> 00:15:36.736
To confirm. the Griffin was not
boarded by an alien intruder.

222
00:15:36.803 --> 00:15:39.906
struck by a viral infection
or any unknown cosmic anomaly.

223
00:15:40.007 --> 00:15:41.641
Affirmative.

224
00:15:41.774 --> 00:15:43.676
Then why were the bodies
removed from the Griffin?

225
00:15:43.776 --> 00:15:46.046
What did Captain Taggert specify
in his orders?

226
00:15:46.113 --> 00:15:48.581
All bodies were transported

227
00:15:48.648 --> 00:15:51.318
by Chief Security Officer
Rose Harper.

228
00:15:51.451 --> 00:15:53.620
including the body
of the captain.

229
00:15:53.720 --> 00:15:56.889
Computer. tell me everything
on record about Harper.

230
00:15:57.724 --> 00:15:59.359
Graduated top of her class.

231
00:15:59.459 --> 00:16:01.494
Rose Harper was known
to be detail-oriented.

232
00:16:01.628 --> 00:16:03.130
driven and ambitious.

233
00:16:03.263 --> 00:16:05.665
Sound like anyone you know?

234
00:16:07.400 --> 00:16:09.469
Before the Griffin disappeared.

235
00:16:09.569 --> 00:16:11.671
Harper filed numerous
security reports

236
00:16:11.771 --> 00:16:15.075
about "erratic behavior"
spreading among the crew.

237
00:16:15.142 --> 00:16:16.476
Erratic?

238
00:16:16.576 --> 00:16:18.445
Violent outbursts.

239
00:16:18.545 --> 00:16:19.846
Self-harm. delusions.

240
00:16:19.979 --> 00:16:22.549
She reported each
to her superiors and medical.

241
00:16:22.649 --> 00:16:24.117
Everyone was thoroughly examined

242
00:16:24.217 --> 00:16:25.985
but medically cleared for duty.

243
00:16:26.786 --> 00:16:28.955
So. was she imagining
these incidents?

244
00:16:29.022 --> 00:16:30.990
Well. she certainly
didn't believe so.

245
00:16:31.091 --> 00:16:32.859
She added the doctor
to her list.

246
00:16:32.992 --> 00:16:34.494
And then the captain
after she believed

247
00:16:34.594 --> 00:16:36.029
he was blocking her reports
to Starfleet.

248
00:16:36.129 --> 00:16:37.997
As the cases spread ship-wide.

249
00:16:38.131 --> 00:16:40.633
Harper took radical steps.

250
00:16:40.733 --> 00:16:43.203
How radical?

251
00:16:50.377 --> 00:16:51.878
How did they all die?

252
00:16:52.011 --> 00:16:53.913
13 strangulations.

253
00:16:54.013 --> 00:16:56.183
Eight stabbings.

254
00:16:56.283 --> 00:16:59.552
287 were transported
into open space

255
00:16:59.686 --> 00:17:02.222
while they were still alive.

256
00:17:04.022 --> 00:17:05.892
La'An. this is Spock.

257
00:17:05.992 --> 00:17:07.827
I have uncovered troubling
information about the survivor

258
00:17:07.926 --> 00:17:10.262
we encountered
and recommend immediate...

259
00:17:15.102 --> 00:17:17.436
Computer. open doors.

260
00:17:19.005 --> 00:17:21.040
Computer.

261
00:17:21.874 --> 00:17:24.743
I need assistance in sickbay.

262
00:17:27.414 --> 00:17:29.549
La'An?

263
00:17:31.251 --> 00:17:33.420
Jim. do you copy?

264
00:18:03.015 --> 00:18:04.417
Harper's personal log.

265
00:18:04.517 --> 00:18:06.919
Stardate... I don't know.

266
00:18:07.053 --> 00:18:09.356
The days are beginning
to bleed together.

267
00:18:09.422 --> 00:18:13.226
Captain Taggert and Dr. G'har
relieved me of duty.

268
00:18:13.293 --> 00:18:14.961
Confined me to quarters.

269
00:18:15.094 --> 00:18:16.396
No one believes me.

270
00:18:16.463 --> 00:18:19.399
But something is wrong
with this ship.

271
00:18:19.499 --> 00:18:21.968
Something is taking over
the crew.

272
00:18:25.705 --> 00:18:28.040
No transportation residue.

273
00:18:29.108 --> 00:18:31.478
And yet...

274
00:19:13.353 --> 00:19:15.755
Spock?

275
00:19:18.991 --> 00:19:21.361
I need you to hear me.

276
00:19:21.461 --> 00:19:23.830
I need you to believe me.

277
00:19:26.533 --> 00:19:30.537
You can't trust any of them.
La'An.

278
00:19:35.642 --> 00:19:37.377
James.

279
00:19:37.510 --> 00:19:39.446
James. we need
to get off this ship now.

280
00:19:39.512 --> 00:19:41.448
Yeah.

281
00:19:41.548 --> 00:19:44.217
About that.

282
00:19:44.351 --> 00:19:46.786
Oh. my God.

283
00:19:49.522 --> 00:19:51.758
That's our shuttle.

284
00:20:05.638 --> 00:20:07.907
It is cold.

285
00:20:09.442 --> 00:20:13.145
I was counseling a patient.
There was a light.

286
00:20:13.280 --> 00:20:15.748
Then darkness.

287
00:20:15.848 --> 00:20:18.050
Then I could not breathe.

288
00:20:18.818 --> 00:20:21.388
Then I was in this bag.

289
00:20:21.454 --> 00:20:23.790
I do not understand what is...

290
00:20:25.157 --> 00:20:27.494
This... this is a dream.

291
00:20:27.594 --> 00:20:30.162
- Fascinating.
- I am having a nightmare.

292
00:20:30.297 --> 00:20:33.099
Why is Spock in my nightmare?

293
00:20:33.165 --> 00:20:35.335
These readings indicate
a living. breathing Vulcan.

294
00:20:35.435 --> 00:20:38.170
I will wake up and be safe.

295
00:20:38.271 --> 00:20:40.307
Perhaps it is a psychic
projection of some kind.

296
00:20:40.407 --> 00:20:42.208
Which puts the reliability
of my observations

297
00:20:42.309 --> 00:20:44.577
and faculties
in considerable doubt.

298
00:20:50.850 --> 00:20:52.719
This is deeply unsettling.

299
00:20:53.486 --> 00:20:55.221
On that. we are in agreement.

300
00:20:56.088 --> 00:20:57.557
What is happening?

301
00:20:57.657 --> 00:20:59.191
I do not know for certain.

302
00:20:59.292 --> 00:21:01.361
My current theory is
that an unknown phenomenon

303
00:21:01.494 --> 00:21:03.696
with a psychotropic area
of effect is causing anyone

304
00:21:03.830 --> 00:21:05.465
- who boards the Griffin to...
- The Griffin?

305
00:21:05.565 --> 00:21:08.267
Why am I on a missing
Federation ship?

306
00:21:08.368 --> 00:21:10.102
You are not.

307
00:21:10.169 --> 00:21:14.106
Spock. I am not an illusion.

308
00:21:14.173 --> 00:21:16.208
Then what are you?

309
00:21:20.146 --> 00:21:22.449
No sign of any ship in the area.

310
00:21:22.515 --> 00:21:24.351
So what blew up our shuttle?

311
00:21:24.484 --> 00:21:26.319
Here's what I know.
Spock was right.

312
00:21:26.419 --> 00:21:29.356
The Griffin is
Division 12's problem to solve.

313
00:21:30.156 --> 00:21:32.359
We only have 20 minutes
of life support left. James.

314
00:21:32.459 --> 00:21:34.026
Don't forget
the Griffin's escape pods

315
00:21:34.160 --> 00:21:36.195
and shuttles are gone.
and we also have a psychopath

316
00:21:36.295 --> 00:21:38.064
who can walk through walls
on board.

317
00:21:38.197 --> 00:21:39.999
We can't just
sit around and wait

318
00:21:40.099 --> 00:21:42.602
for the long-range message
Spock sent to reach Enterprise.

319
00:21:46.072 --> 00:21:48.808
If we can get more power
to comms up here.

320
00:21:48.875 --> 00:21:51.678
I think I can get an SOS signal
to anyone in the neighborhood.

321
00:21:51.744 --> 00:21:53.980
Yes. all right. okay. I'll have
Spock meet me in engineering.

322
00:21:54.046 --> 00:21:56.082
and we'll reroute power
and life support to the bridge.

323
00:21:56.215 --> 00:21:58.050
You think
that'll buy us enough time?

324
00:22:00.853 --> 00:22:02.922
Spock. it's La'An.

325
00:22:03.022 --> 00:22:05.625
I need you
to meet me in engineering.

326
00:22:07.394 --> 00:22:09.261
Why me?

327
00:22:09.396 --> 00:22:12.699
Your theory is that I am
a hallucination. correct?

328
00:22:12.799 --> 00:22:16.736
If that is true. then why did
whatever looked into your mind

329
00:22:16.836 --> 00:22:18.438
choose me to conjure?

330
00:22:18.538 --> 00:22:21.474
I only know
that you are not T'Pring.

331
00:22:23.410 --> 00:22:27.680
When I was on my kahs-wan.
I was injured while hiking.

332
00:22:27.780 --> 00:22:30.282
Wildlife circled me.
waiting to strike.

333
00:22:30.417 --> 00:22:33.553
Trapped.
I experienced what humans

334
00:22:33.653 --> 00:22:36.589
refer to as a... panic attack.

335
00:22:36.689 --> 00:22:39.125
I centered my mind
by meditating.

336
00:22:39.225 --> 00:22:42.762
chanting a favorite couplet
by the great poet Ka'nina.

337
00:22:46.298 --> 00:22:47.500
"It will guide you home."

338
00:22:47.600 --> 00:22:50.970
It brought me back.
and I survived.

339
00:22:52.405 --> 00:22:53.706
You are the only person

340
00:22:53.773 --> 00:22:56.208
I have ever shared
that story with. Spock.

341
00:22:56.308 --> 00:22:58.778
Correct. And since
you are a product of my mind.

342
00:22:58.878 --> 00:23:01.981
you are able to recite the real
T'Pring's anecdote back to me.

343
00:23:04.484 --> 00:23:08.821
Well. one thing we can
both agree on is a shared desire

344
00:23:08.921 --> 00:23:11.323
to disembark this ship
immediately.

345
00:23:12.425 --> 00:23:14.060
And you do not need
to believe that I am real

346
00:23:14.126 --> 00:23:18.865
in order to accept my help
in opening these doors. correct?

347
00:23:35.915 --> 00:23:38.518
All right. All right.

348
00:23:43.890 --> 00:23:47.093
No. no. no. no.
Come on. Come on.

349
00:23:56.368 --> 00:23:59.371
Spock. you need to see this.

350
00:24:04.711 --> 00:24:06.646
I'm the only one
not affected or...

351
00:24:11.651 --> 00:24:16.989
I can't let what happened here
spread throughout Starfleet.

352
00:24:21.293 --> 00:24:25.064
Whatever happened here. it drove
the Griffin CSO mad. Look.

353
00:24:25.164 --> 00:24:30.637
I can't let what happened here
spread throughout Starfleet.

354
00:24:30.737 --> 00:24:32.572
You know what must be done.

355
00:24:36.408 --> 00:24:38.511
Harper.

356
00:24:38.611 --> 00:24:41.147
What happened to you?

357
00:24:41.247 --> 00:24:45.184
The very same thing that is
happening to you right now.

358
00:25:00.700 --> 00:25:02.101
Damn it.

359
00:25:52.518 --> 00:25:54.687
Dada?

360
00:26:03.295 --> 00:26:04.664
Hello?

361
00:26:08.701 --> 00:26:10.302
Can you hear me?

362
00:26:31.290 --> 00:26:33.860
No. wait. Wait!

363
00:26:33.960 --> 00:26:36.128
Dada?

364
00:26:37.129 --> 00:26:38.798
David?

365
00:26:39.632 --> 00:26:41.834
Sever the green. then red.

366
00:26:45.872 --> 00:26:47.807
The color scheme of these wires.

367
00:26:47.874 --> 00:26:51.043
Does it look familiar to you?

368
00:26:53.545 --> 00:26:55.414
The holiday spent on Hurk'ah.

369
00:26:55.514 --> 00:26:57.149
A trip you surprised me with.

370
00:26:57.216 --> 00:26:59.151
Do you also recall what I said

371
00:26:59.218 --> 00:27:01.587
when you told me
of the plans to go?

372
00:27:02.354 --> 00:27:04.523
That you do not care
for surprises.

373
00:27:04.623 --> 00:27:06.726
It was too human an exercise.

374
00:27:06.826 --> 00:27:08.995
I should not have said that.

375
00:27:10.697 --> 00:27:12.765
It was a wonderful trip.

376
00:27:13.565 --> 00:27:15.334
I have sought counseling
to understand

377
00:27:15.434 --> 00:27:18.570
what caused our engagement
to dissolve.

378
00:27:18.671 --> 00:27:21.007
- The reason for that was my...
- My fault.

379
00:27:21.908 --> 00:27:25.277
I did not love you
as you deserved to be loved.

380
00:27:29.581 --> 00:27:31.784
I do not know
what caused you and I

381
00:27:31.884 --> 00:27:34.153
to be in this place
at this time.

382
00:27:34.253 --> 00:27:36.622
But I do know
what it can give us.

383
00:27:41.360 --> 00:27:42.795
A second chance.

384
00:27:53.706 --> 00:27:59.345
That itch that's
been gnawing at you for months?

385
00:28:09.221 --> 00:28:13.059
That feeling that something
is wrong with you?

386
00:28:22.568 --> 00:28:24.837
La'An Noonien-Singh.

387
00:28:24.971 --> 00:28:27.006
you are not a Khan.

388
00:28:27.106 --> 00:28:29.041
You are not a Romulan.

389
00:28:29.141 --> 00:28:33.679
And you are not a monster.

390
00:28:49.595 --> 00:28:52.664
You're one of us.

391
00:29:06.545 --> 00:29:10.282
I could not see it clearly
until we were parted.

392
00:29:10.349 --> 00:29:13.953
Your humanity
is not your weakness.

393
00:29:14.020 --> 00:29:16.188
It is your biggest strength.

394
00:29:20.793 --> 00:29:23.229
What has held you back
in your relationships

395
00:29:23.362 --> 00:29:25.798
and even your beloved Starfleet

396
00:29:25.865 --> 00:29:28.567
is your Vulcan side.

397
00:29:31.070 --> 00:29:34.140
But here on the Griffin.

398
00:29:34.240 --> 00:29:36.375
we can fix that. Spock.

399
00:29:36.475 --> 00:29:37.743
No. wait.

400
00:29:37.844 --> 00:29:40.046
- We can set you...
- Wait!

401
00:29:41.213 --> 00:29:45.617
Free.

402
00:29:50.857 --> 00:29:54.326
David! David!

403
00:30:11.978 --> 00:30:13.946
You got Spock's message.

404
00:30:14.080 --> 00:30:17.749
Captain set course
as soon as we received it.

405
00:30:17.816 --> 00:30:19.618
The Griffin.

406
00:30:19.718 --> 00:30:22.621
After all this time.
Kirk. what happened?

407
00:30:22.754 --> 00:30:24.723
I think Jim's had enough
for one day. Ortegas.

408
00:30:24.823 --> 00:30:26.725
We'll investigate after we get
him to Dr. M'Benga.

409
00:30:26.792 --> 00:30:28.027
Number One?

410
00:30:28.127 --> 00:30:29.495
Scotty.
lock onto Kirk's signature

411
00:30:29.628 --> 00:30:31.530
and transport him
directly to sickbay.

412
00:30:31.630 --> 00:30:32.798
Uh. wait. Captain.

413
00:30:32.899 --> 00:30:35.434
Uh. there's someone else
on board.

414
00:30:35.501 --> 00:30:37.469
a survivor named Harper.

415
00:30:37.569 --> 00:30:39.105
Enterprise. do you copy?

416
00:30:41.073 --> 00:30:43.442
Uhura. since our communicators
aren't working...

417
00:30:43.542 --> 00:30:45.011
Sir.

418
00:30:45.111 --> 00:30:47.246
this comms station is...

419
00:30:47.313 --> 00:30:49.715
Well...

420
00:30:49.815 --> 00:30:52.851
I had to dig through there.

421
00:30:52.985 --> 00:30:55.087
I'm sorry.

422
00:30:55.154 --> 00:30:58.524
I heard something.

423
00:30:58.624 --> 00:31:00.592
Someone... inside the console.

424
00:31:02.828 --> 00:31:05.531
Was it the survivor? Harper?

425
00:31:06.332 --> 00:31:09.969
I... I heard David.

426
00:31:11.003 --> 00:31:12.771
Your son?

427
00:31:15.607 --> 00:31:18.844
Jim. he's on his way
to Epsilon-5.

428
00:31:19.611 --> 00:31:22.148
Carol waited
as long as she could.

429
00:31:22.881 --> 00:31:26.152
But in her defense. you did say
you'd be home three days ago.

430
00:31:29.555 --> 00:31:31.023
Sir. we have
to get off this ship

431
00:31:31.157 --> 00:31:33.225
before whatever's affecting me
affects you all.

432
00:31:33.359 --> 00:31:35.127
All right. everybody. how
do we get back to Enterprise?

433
00:31:35.194 --> 00:31:36.262
Best idea wins. Go.

434
00:31:36.362 --> 00:31:38.030
Spacewalk? Tethered to the ship?

435
00:31:38.164 --> 00:31:40.032
Fun. but EV suits on the
Griffin are unaccounted for.

436
00:31:41.500 --> 00:31:43.970
Telemetry array
is still operational.

437
00:31:44.070 --> 00:31:47.139
Gets us in the
ballpark for a transporter signal.

438
00:32:02.721 --> 00:32:04.423
Jim?

439
00:32:04.556 --> 00:32:06.392
Hey. maybe you should
have a seat. huh?

440
00:32:06.492 --> 00:32:07.859
Come on.

441
00:32:09.461 --> 00:32:11.530
They're going
to find La'An and Spock.

442
00:32:11.630 --> 00:32:15.901
Uhura thinks that she can
transport us off one at a time.

443
00:32:16.002 --> 00:32:17.869
Take a minute.

444
00:32:17.936 --> 00:32:20.539
When your head is clear...

445
00:32:20.606 --> 00:32:22.474
get to the transporter.

446
00:32:26.478 --> 00:32:28.114
Sam.

447
00:32:30.016 --> 00:32:32.118
I don't know
what's wrong with me.

448
00:32:36.922 --> 00:32:39.058
I don't know either.

449
00:32:39.158 --> 00:32:41.660
But you're gonna be okay.

450
00:32:54.240 --> 00:32:55.741
Bridge.

451
00:33:01.447 --> 00:33:04.350
Deck 17.

452
00:33:07.486 --> 00:33:10.156
Let's try that again. shall we?

453
00:33:10.256 --> 00:33:12.424
Bridge.

454
00:33:18.997 --> 00:33:22.334
Deck 17.

455
00:33:24.836 --> 00:33:26.638
Computer. bridge.

456
00:33:38.284 --> 00:33:41.320
Deck 17...

457
00:33:41.420 --> 00:33:43.622
La'An.

458
00:35:06.938 --> 00:35:08.907
It's all my fault.

459
00:35:27.526 --> 00:35:30.629
It was my job
to keep the crew safe.

460
00:35:41.707 --> 00:35:44.142
And I failed.

461
00:35:44.276 --> 00:35:46.845
But it's not too late for you.

462
00:36:04.129 --> 00:36:05.597
La'An?

463
00:36:05.697 --> 00:36:06.965
La'An. hey.

464
00:36:07.098 --> 00:36:08.634
Come here. Oh.

465
00:36:08.734 --> 00:36:10.101
Oh.

466
00:36:10.902 --> 00:36:14.273
Whatever happened here must be
really bad if you're hugging.

467
00:36:14.373 --> 00:36:15.941
Let's get the hell out of here.

468
00:36:16.007 --> 00:36:19.211
Yeah. There's our girl.
Come on.

469
00:36:23.014 --> 00:36:24.516
Friend of yours?

470
00:36:24.650 --> 00:36:26.718
Not in the slightest.

471
00:36:31.022 --> 00:36:32.658
Our love died

472
00:36:32.758 --> 00:36:35.093
because your heart

473
00:36:35.160 --> 00:36:39.398
was not in the right place.

474
00:36:44.002 --> 00:36:46.171
Let's change that. shall we?

475
00:36:49.641 --> 00:36:51.243
No.

476
00:36:51.343 --> 00:36:53.078
No. stop.

477
00:36:54.179 --> 00:36:55.614
Spock. is that you?

478
00:36:55.714 --> 00:36:57.215
Captain! Help!

479
00:36:59.017 --> 00:37:00.619
Easy. We've got you.

480
00:37:00.686 --> 00:37:03.088
You're safe now. you understand?

481
00:37:03.889 --> 00:37:05.857
T'Pring. she tied me down.

482
00:37:05.957 --> 00:37:07.326
T'Pring?

483
00:37:07.426 --> 00:37:09.461
As in your ex T'Pring?

484
00:37:09.561 --> 00:37:11.563
She is dangerous.

485
00:37:11.663 --> 00:37:14.433
You know. I never liked her.

486
00:37:16.335 --> 00:37:17.936
All right.

487
00:37:18.870 --> 00:37:21.873
- Let's roll.
- All right.

488
00:37:21.973 --> 00:37:24.576
Oh. Who's this little guy?

489
00:37:25.511 --> 00:37:27.813
Reminds me of the tchotchkes

490
00:37:27.913 --> 00:37:30.916
Dad used to bring home
when he was home on leave.

491
00:37:31.016 --> 00:37:33.051
Like some kind of.
I don't know...

492
00:37:33.151 --> 00:37:35.654
Apology for not being around.

493
00:37:35.754 --> 00:37:37.389
I have more of these
crappy little things

494
00:37:37.489 --> 00:37:41.059
in a box somewhere than I have
memories of playing with Dad.

495
00:37:42.761 --> 00:37:45.631
I mean. when was the last time
you even heard from the old man?

496
00:37:46.565 --> 00:37:49.234
- Birthday.
- Birthday. Right.

497
00:37:49.335 --> 00:37:51.370
How do you do it. Sam?

498
00:37:52.103 --> 00:37:55.907
How do you balance
Starfleet and family?

499
00:37:56.908 --> 00:37:58.310
Well. I...

500
00:37:59.177 --> 00:38:00.612
I don't.

501
00:38:01.347 --> 00:38:03.682
But I get home
as often as I can.

502
00:38:03.782 --> 00:38:05.717
And every night I call my boys.

503
00:38:05.817 --> 00:38:08.387
sign off with the same thing.

504
00:38:09.154 --> 00:38:10.589
"Good night. I love you.

505
00:38:10.689 --> 00:38:12.758
and I'll see you
in your dreams."

506
00:38:15.427 --> 00:38:18.263
We get out of here
safe and sound.

507
00:38:18.364 --> 00:38:20.732
I'm gonna do that for David.

508
00:38:21.567 --> 00:38:23.735
So let's get out of here. then.

509
00:38:23.802 --> 00:38:25.537
Dad.

510
00:38:25.604 --> 00:38:27.005
Wait.

511
00:38:27.806 --> 00:38:29.274
Wait. do you hear that?

512
00:38:29.375 --> 00:38:31.877
- Dad.
- Is that... is that Peter?

513
00:38:31.943 --> 00:38:34.212
Whoa. whoa. Hey. hey. hey. Sam.
It's not real.

514
00:38:34.279 --> 00:38:36.948
- It's not real.
- No. no. That's my little boy. That's my boy.

515
00:38:37.048 --> 00:38:38.917
Sam. Sam. listen to me.

516
00:38:38.984 --> 00:38:41.453
It's not real.

517
00:38:41.587 --> 00:38:42.588
Okay.

518
00:38:42.688 --> 00:38:44.189
We have to get out of here now.

519
00:38:44.289 --> 00:38:46.392
- Come on. Let's go.
- Okay.

520
00:38:53.131 --> 00:38:55.634
Ready room. We can get out...

521
00:39:00.005 --> 00:39:01.473
Okay. we're set.

522
00:39:01.607 --> 00:39:03.842
But I was right. We can
only transport one at a time.

523
00:39:03.975 --> 00:39:05.777
We have to get
you two out of here first

524
00:39:05.844 --> 00:39:07.045
before Harper finds us

525
00:39:07.145 --> 00:39:08.847
or this ship affects you
as it has me.

526
00:39:08.980 --> 00:39:11.683
- No arguments. You understand?
- Who's arguing?

527
00:39:13.084 --> 00:39:14.920
Get me off this dump.

528
00:39:19.491 --> 00:39:21.727
Wait. No.

529
00:39:21.827 --> 00:39:23.194
Something's wrong.

530
00:39:30.335 --> 00:39:31.737
Let me...

531
00:39:32.771 --> 00:39:35.306
- What did you do?
- What? No. I...

532
00:39:37.476 --> 00:39:39.110
- I...
- Erica! Hang on.

533
00:39:39.177 --> 00:39:40.946
I'm transporting you
into the buffer.

534
00:39:52.958 --> 00:39:56.327
You set the transporter
to beam Erica into herself.

535
00:39:56.428 --> 00:39:57.563
To fuse her.

536
00:39:57.663 --> 00:39:59.030
Nyota. let me explain.
Please. I...

537
00:39:59.130 --> 00:40:00.632
- No. No.
- Nyota.

538
00:40:00.699 --> 00:40:03.234
- Oh. my God.
- Nyota.

539
00:40:05.070 --> 00:40:06.872
Clearly.
something is manipulating

540
00:40:06.972 --> 00:40:08.674
whoever boards the Griffin.

541
00:40:08.740 --> 00:40:10.809
We must get you both
off this malignant ship.

542
00:40:10.909 --> 00:40:12.243
Easy. easy. easy.

543
00:40:12.377 --> 00:40:14.112
What did Pike tell you?

544
00:40:20.519 --> 00:40:22.988
You're safe now. Spock.

545
00:40:23.088 --> 00:40:24.656
No.

546
00:40:26.024 --> 00:40:28.059
You just need
to listen to the ship.

547
00:40:28.193 --> 00:40:29.661
I mean...

548
00:40:29.728 --> 00:40:31.830
can't you hear it?

549
00:40:32.698 --> 00:40:34.733
All it wants to do
is set us free.

550
00:40:36.334 --> 00:40:38.403
Una. with your enhanced Illyrian
blood. you should be able

551
00:40:38.504 --> 00:40:39.705
- to fight off...
- My blood

552
00:40:39.805 --> 00:40:41.673
is what's been
holding me back. Spock.

553
00:40:41.740 --> 00:40:43.174
Starfleet will never
promote me to captain

554
00:40:43.241 --> 00:40:45.010
as long as I'm an Illyrian.

555
00:40:45.110 --> 00:40:46.812
But here...

556
00:40:46.912 --> 00:40:49.180
I can be free of that.

557
00:40:49.247 --> 00:40:51.483
Una. please do not!

558
00:41:22.113 --> 00:41:26.017
We're never getting
off this ship. are we?

559
00:41:34.325 --> 00:41:36.662
We're gonna die.

560
00:41:37.529 --> 00:41:39.565
Out here...

561
00:41:39.631 --> 00:41:41.499
in space.

562
00:41:42.634 --> 00:41:44.469
Alone.

563
00:41:45.503 --> 00:41:47.773
Like Kirks are born to do.

564
00:41:47.873 --> 00:41:50.008
Sam. listen to me.

565
00:41:57.949 --> 00:41:59.017
Sam?

566
00:41:59.150 --> 00:42:00.852
Help me with the door.

567
00:42:00.986 --> 00:42:02.320
Sam!

568
00:42:03.589 --> 00:42:04.690
Sam!

569
00:42:04.823 --> 00:42:07.993
Sam. it's gonna break.
It's gonna break!

570
00:42:08.126 --> 00:42:10.161
Get away from it.

571
00:42:12.230 --> 00:42:14.132
My brother.

572
00:42:14.232 --> 00:42:16.467
Always the hero.

573
00:42:17.168 --> 00:42:18.970
But you can't save everyone.

574
00:42:19.738 --> 00:42:22.708
You have to make peace
with that. Jim.

575
00:42:23.709 --> 00:42:26.177
Sam. it's the ship.
Don't listen to it.

576
00:42:26.311 --> 00:42:28.179
- Until you accept that...
- Don't listen to it.

577
00:42:28.279 --> 00:42:31.683
You will never be free.

578
00:42:31.817 --> 00:42:33.284
But don't worry.

579
00:42:33.384 --> 00:42:35.386
The Griffin's gonna
show you the way.

580
00:42:40.491 --> 00:42:42.794
No!

581
00:42:42.894 --> 00:42:44.295
No!

582
00:42:44.362 --> 00:42:46.898
Sam. Sam.

583
00:42:52.303 --> 00:42:53.705
Jim.

584
00:42:54.505 --> 00:42:56.541
Tell my babies good night.

585
00:42:56.675 --> 00:42:59.477
That I love them.

586
00:42:59.544 --> 00:43:01.379
And I'll see them in their...

587
00:43:02.681 --> 00:43:04.082
No!

588
00:43:06.217 --> 00:43:08.119
No!

589
00:43:15.526 --> 00:43:17.528
Nyota. listen to me. please.

590
00:43:17.629 --> 00:43:20.465
I need to get you off this ship.

591
00:43:23.534 --> 00:43:24.535
Nyota.

592
00:43:24.602 --> 00:43:26.171
Look at yourself. La'An.

593
00:43:26.271 --> 00:43:28.006
Something isn't right.

594
00:43:28.073 --> 00:43:29.307
No.

595
00:43:29.407 --> 00:43:31.943
Something is definitely
not right.

596
00:43:32.043 --> 00:43:34.045
But Ortegas is alive
and safe in the buffer.

597
00:43:34.145 --> 00:43:36.514
and I need your help
to get us back to Enterprise

598
00:43:36.581 --> 00:43:38.083
so we can save her.

599
00:43:40.618 --> 00:43:42.153
Please. Nyota.

600
00:43:43.722 --> 00:43:45.791
What is wrong with this place?

601
00:43:46.591 --> 00:43:47.759
Look out.

602
00:43:58.036 --> 00:43:59.570
It's time to let go. La'An.

603
00:43:59.637 --> 00:44:03.709
On the Griffin. you can
finally be your true self.

604
00:44:05.210 --> 00:44:07.112
I mean...

605
00:44:08.714 --> 00:44:11.449
look what you've
accomplished here already.

606
00:44:14.252 --> 00:44:16.454
Please don't
kill me. La'An. Please.

607
00:44:16.587 --> 00:44:18.824
Please. please.

608
00:44:18.957 --> 00:44:20.992
Please don't kill me.

609
00:44:47.152 --> 00:44:48.920
Welcome home.

610
00:44:58.764 --> 00:45:00.131
La'An.

611
00:45:02.333 --> 00:45:04.002
Thank God you're okay.

612
00:45:04.135 --> 00:45:06.738
Listen to me. we have to get
to the transporter.

613
00:45:12.277 --> 00:45:13.444
Tell me you don't hear that.

614
00:45:19.284 --> 00:45:21.987
I hear everything now.

615
00:45:34.499 --> 00:45:36.367
This ship is amazing. Spock.

616
00:45:37.168 --> 00:45:40.438
I mean.
all the freshest ingredients.

617
00:45:43.308 --> 00:45:45.877
If I stay on board
the Griffin...

618
00:45:47.512 --> 00:45:49.815
I can be free of my fate.

619
00:45:49.881 --> 00:45:51.682
I don't have to be
the captain anymore.

620
00:45:54.419 --> 00:45:57.122
I can be the head chef.

621
00:46:15.373 --> 00:46:18.543
Whatever you are. please...

622
00:46:19.344 --> 00:46:20.946
let them go.

623
00:46:21.746 --> 00:46:23.882
Let them go and take me.

624
00:46:23.982 --> 00:46:26.651
Ever so noble.

625
00:46:27.518 --> 00:46:30.121
Ever so logical.

626
00:46:31.056 --> 00:46:33.892
But logic has no place here.

627
00:46:35.994 --> 00:46:40.899
And yet that is what you have
inadvertently brought to me.

628
00:46:47.138 --> 00:46:48.639
What are you doing?

629
00:46:50.808 --> 00:46:53.411
"It will guide you home."

630
00:47:51.002 --> 00:47:52.137
The ship picked Harper.

631
00:47:52.270 --> 00:47:54.639
and now it's picked us.

632
00:47:54.739 --> 00:47:57.275
The Griffin needs
a captain. James.

633
00:47:57.375 --> 00:47:58.643
And who better to captain

634
00:47:58.743 --> 00:48:00.678
a ship of the damned
than a Kirk?

635
00:48:00.811 --> 00:48:02.647
This isn't you.

636
00:48:02.780 --> 00:48:04.682
This isn't you.

637
00:48:04.815 --> 00:48:06.517
This is me.

638
00:48:07.885 --> 00:48:09.020
The real me.

639
00:48:11.589 --> 00:48:16.561
And you can feel this way. too.
if you just let go.

640
00:48:18.063 --> 00:48:20.665
Why won't you let go?

641
00:48:24.369 --> 00:48:26.337
David.

642
00:48:40.018 --> 00:48:41.719
Your little boy

643
00:48:41.852 --> 00:48:45.056
is going to die just like you.

644
00:48:45.190 --> 00:48:47.825
At the end of a blade.

645
00:48:47.892 --> 00:48:52.063
Bleeding out
in a dark corner of space.

646
00:49:11.549 --> 00:49:13.051
It's okay.

647
00:49:13.851 --> 00:49:16.921
You're okay. You're okay.

648
00:49:36.241 --> 00:49:37.742
- My...
- Jim.

649
00:49:37.842 --> 00:49:39.510
- My...
- Oh.

650
00:49:39.610 --> 00:49:42.113
My b... my brother Sam.

651
00:49:42.913 --> 00:49:44.515
Is he. is he okay?

652
00:49:44.615 --> 00:49:46.217
Your brother?

653
00:49:46.317 --> 00:49:48.253
He's on shore leave
visiting his family.

654
00:49:48.353 --> 00:49:50.121
Jim.

655
00:49:50.921 --> 00:49:52.590
Jim. Jim.

656
00:50:09.607 --> 00:50:12.110
So. what
will become of the Griffin?

657
00:50:12.210 --> 00:50:13.444
Well. the USS Thorn has arrived

658
00:50:13.578 --> 00:50:15.046
to tow the ship
back to wherever the hell

659
00:50:15.146 --> 00:50:18.316
Division 12's base of operations
is located.

660
00:50:19.150 --> 00:50:20.718
How many cases
have you referred to them

661
00:50:20.818 --> 00:50:22.487
in your career. Chris?

662
00:50:22.620 --> 00:50:24.055
Six.

663
00:50:24.122 --> 00:50:25.723
Four were resolved
with scientific

664
00:50:25.823 --> 00:50:27.558
or alien explanations.

665
00:50:28.426 --> 00:50:29.860
And the other two?

666
00:50:31.629 --> 00:50:33.698
I'll let you know
when I find out.

667
00:50:34.499 --> 00:50:35.866
So. how's Jim?

668
00:50:36.634 --> 00:50:38.269
He's healing well.

669
00:50:38.336 --> 00:50:40.071
But he was truly convinced
that you and the boarding party

670
00:50:40.138 --> 00:50:42.740
actually beamed
onto the Griffin.

671
00:50:42.807 --> 00:50:45.009
And Spock and La'An?

672
00:50:49.947 --> 00:50:52.750
Physically. they're all fine.

673
00:50:52.817 --> 00:50:54.219
Mentally?

674
00:51:03.761 --> 00:51:04.962
Good as new.

675
00:51:05.029 --> 00:51:08.333
And just as pointy
as I remember.

676
00:51:10.835 --> 00:51:12.570
How do they feel?

677
00:51:17.175 --> 00:51:18.776
They feel like me.

678
00:51:19.544 --> 00:51:22.347
I'll pass your compliments
on to the chef.

679
00:51:25.015 --> 00:51:27.051
Thank you for coming
to my quarters. Christine.

680
00:51:27.152 --> 00:51:28.819
I recognize
the request was illogical.

681
00:51:28.919 --> 00:51:30.321
but after what transpired
on the Griffin...

682
00:51:30.388 --> 00:51:32.957
Sickbay was the last place
you wanted to be?

683
00:51:33.057 --> 00:51:36.494
I hate eating in the mess hall
for the same reason.

684
00:51:36.561 --> 00:51:39.497
During the war.
I was briefly stationed

685
00:51:39.597 --> 00:51:41.999
at the hospital on Yrti.

686
00:51:42.099 --> 00:51:43.701
I am sorry to hear that.

687
00:51:43.801 --> 00:51:45.636
The Yrti offensive
took heavy casualties.

688
00:51:45.703 --> 00:51:48.839
When the OR got blasted.
we had to triage

689
00:51:48.939 --> 00:51:51.309
and operate in the mess.

690
00:51:52.477 --> 00:51:54.879
Wasn't the most appetizing place
to begin with.

691
00:51:55.012 --> 00:51:58.683
but... after that night...

692
00:52:04.155 --> 00:52:05.790
Are you okay?

693
00:52:10.395 --> 00:52:12.463
I am fine. Christine.

694
00:52:18.603 --> 00:52:22.006
Thank you for making
this "house call."

695
00:52:22.072 --> 00:52:23.474
Of course.

696
00:52:29.914 --> 00:52:32.116
Can I ask one question?

697
00:52:34.352 --> 00:52:36.086
Why T'Pring?

698
00:52:36.221 --> 00:52:38.589
I believe whatever probed
my mind selected her

699
00:52:38.689 --> 00:52:42.193
to extract the most
emotional response it could.

700
00:52:42.293 --> 00:52:44.929
But the illusion was powered
by my own memories.

701
00:52:45.029 --> 00:52:46.797
My own beliefs.

702
00:52:47.632 --> 00:52:50.301
That anchored me.
Brought me back.

703
00:52:50.401 --> 00:52:52.370
To her?

704
00:52:54.372 --> 00:52:55.940
To logic.

705
00:53:00.144 --> 00:53:02.079
I don't understand.
What's the problem?

706
00:53:02.179 --> 00:53:04.949
The problem. sir.
is that your report

707
00:53:05.082 --> 00:53:09.387
on the Griffin incident is.
is missing some key data.

708
00:53:09.454 --> 00:53:10.988
Like what?

709
00:53:11.756 --> 00:53:15.293
Like the fact that I tried
to kill James Kirk?

710
00:53:16.827 --> 00:53:18.929
Have you talked to him?
Or Spock?

711
00:53:20.565 --> 00:53:21.932
No.

712
00:53:22.767 --> 00:53:24.602
Okay.

713
00:53:24.702 --> 00:53:26.003
Have a seat and have a drink.

714
00:53:26.103 --> 00:53:29.374
Don't make me
make that an order.

715
00:53:47.658 --> 00:53:49.994
James saw his son.

716
00:53:50.127 --> 00:53:51.462
Spock his ex.

717
00:53:51.529 --> 00:53:53.331
And you're wondering
why you saw Harper.

718
00:53:53.431 --> 00:53:56.033
No. I know why.

719
00:53:57.268 --> 00:53:59.036
Starfleet is my family.

720
00:53:59.804 --> 00:54:03.207
I just want to know
what happened to the crew.

721
00:54:03.341 --> 00:54:05.543
To Harper.

722
00:54:06.911 --> 00:54:09.580
Ever tell you about
my Uncle Art's farm?

723
00:54:11.215 --> 00:54:13.083
- Sir?
- It's a beautiful thing.

724
00:54:13.183 --> 00:54:14.218
35 acres.

725
00:54:14.352 --> 00:54:17.121
And it had this old creaky barn

726
00:54:17.187 --> 00:54:19.557
that my cousins swore
was haunted

727
00:54:19.690 --> 00:54:22.226
by a woman carrying a scythe.

728
00:54:22.993 --> 00:54:27.332
And I slept out in that barn
to prove it was all nonsense.

729
00:54:27.432 --> 00:54:29.099
And I was right.

730
00:54:30.501 --> 00:54:32.069
Till I wasn't.

731
00:54:32.870 --> 00:54:35.139
Just before I drifted off...

732
00:54:36.240 --> 00:54:39.877
I heard steel

733
00:54:39.977 --> 00:54:42.813
scraping across the floor

734
00:54:42.880 --> 00:54:46.717
and a-a voice that whispered.

735
00:54:46.817 --> 00:54:49.987
"I know your true name."

736
00:54:50.054 --> 00:54:52.289
I ran out of there
about as fast as I could.

737
00:54:52.390 --> 00:54:54.625
Cut my arm on a nail
on the way out.

738
00:54:54.725 --> 00:54:56.894
Now. come sunrise.
my family searched that barn

739
00:54:56.994 --> 00:55:00.431
top to bottom.
didn't find a damn thing.

740
00:55:01.732 --> 00:55:03.634
But I still have that scar.

741
00:55:03.734 --> 00:55:06.270
Space is limitless in its beauty

742
00:55:06.371 --> 00:55:08.205
and in its terror.

743
00:55:09.540 --> 00:55:11.709
Whatever you encountered.

744
00:55:11.809 --> 00:55:15.980
the only thing that matters
is that you survived.

745
00:55:21.251 --> 00:55:25.022
And that is all Starfleet
needs to know.

746
00:55:28.258 --> 00:55:29.827
Case closed.

747
00:55:38.102 --> 00:55:39.937
Carol and David
are pretty far out.

748
00:55:40.070 --> 00:55:43.974
so I relayed a signal
off a starbase or two.

749
00:55:44.108 --> 00:55:47.612
Press this button
and you will hail her outpost.

750
00:55:49.947 --> 00:55:51.315
Got it.

751
00:55:52.517 --> 00:55:54.485
And the cookies?

752
00:55:56.554 --> 00:55:58.656
Someone once told me
that refusing

753
00:55:58.789 --> 00:56:01.626
freshly made cookies
is a clear sign of madness.

754
00:56:01.726 --> 00:56:03.394
Mm.

755
00:56:04.228 --> 00:56:07.798
You're worried that I lost
my mind on the Griffin?

756
00:56:07.898 --> 00:56:10.701
If you don't want the cookies.
I'll just...

757
00:56:14.972 --> 00:56:16.674
Are you all right?

758
00:56:24.515 --> 00:56:26.551
Yes.

759
00:56:28.519 --> 00:56:30.988
You're gonna be okay. Jim.

760
00:56:34.759 --> 00:56:36.761
How do you know?

761
00:56:40.765 --> 00:56:42.032
Nyota.

762
00:56:44.969 --> 00:56:47.104
Thank you.

763
00:56:48.005 --> 00:56:50.508
Always happy to be of service.
